326:
(a) Before granting a film permit, the city manager shall review the application and consult with necessary public officers, including, but not limited to, the Hall County sheriff, the fire marshal, and the camera ready liaison and determine whether the proposed film activity will unreasonably interfere with the public health, safety, and general welfare or unreasonably endanger any property. Appropriate city officers and county officers shall be consulted to review the application as deemed necessary by the city manager. When granting a film permit, any reasonable condition may be imposed as necessary to protect public health, safety, general welfare and property. The factors that may be considered when granting or conditioning a permit include, but are not limited to, the following factors: noise, traffic congestion, traffic hazards, environmental concerns, and interference with street maintenance work, unreasonable interference with normal business operations or residential peace and quiet and whether the proposed activity violates federal, state, or local laws or ordinances.
